<newsitem itemid="618999" id="root" date="1997-05-27" xml:lang="en">
<title>GERMANY: Bilfinger details 1996 earnings.</title>
<headline>Bilfinger details 1996 earnings.</headline>
<dateline>MANNHEIM, Germany 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   92	vs 106</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		     147     vs 168</p>
<p>    Group DVFA earnings per share	  3.41    vs 3.96 marks</p>
<p>    Parent net profit			  73.7    vs 84</p>
<p>    Group construction output		9,247   vs 8,573</p>
<p>Of which</p>
<p>     Domestic output			   4,864   vs 4,557</p>
<p>     Foreign output			    4,383   vs 4,016</p>
<p>    Group new orders			   9,942   vs 9,580</p>
<p>Of which</p>
<p>     Domestic new orders		     4,263   vs 5,443</p>
<p>     Foreign new orders			5,679   vs 4,137</p>
<p>    Group orders in hand		     9,979   vs 9,284</p>
<p>Of which</p>
<p>     Domestic orders in hand		 4,211   vs 4,812</p>
<p>     Foreign orders in hand		  5,768   vs 4,472</p>
<p>    Group sales				  7,027   vs 7,038</p>
<p>    Group workforce (at 31.12.96)	  51,171  vs 49,747</p>
<p>Of which</p>
<p>     Domestic				    13,686  vs 14,886</p>
<p>     Foreign				     37,485  vs 34,861</p>
<p>    DVFA cash flow			     327     vs 348</p>
<p>    Group cash flow per share		9.06    vs 9.67</p>
<p>    Group investments			  265     vs 360</p>
<p>Of which</p>
<p>     Domestic				    121     vs 196</p>
<p>     Foreign				     144     vs 164</p>
<p>     Capital investments		     241     vs 291</p>
<p>     Financial investments		   24	vs 69</p>
<p>    Dividend (already announced)	   1.20    vs 1.35 marks</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German construction group is Bilfinger + Berger Bau AG. The group said that the Asia-Pacific region accounted for 50 percent of its foreign construction output. The cash flow figures are calculated under the DVFA German analysts' method.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
